# Admin Assets

## JavaScript (`admin/js/`)

- Wrap in an IIFE with `'use strict'`.
- Guard on `window.edminboostData` before running.
- Scope DOM queries to `.edminboost-wrap` or plugin-specific selectors.
- No jQuery unless WordPress already loads it for the screen.
- Use `DOMContentLoaded` for initialization.
- On ready, set `data-edminboost-ready="true"` on `.edminboost-wrap`.

```javascript
( function () {
	'use strict';

	if ( typeof window.edminboostData === 'undefined' ) {
		return;
	}

	document.addEventListener( 'DOMContentLoaded', function () {
		var root = document.querySelector( '.edminboost-wrap' );
		if ( ! root ) {
			return;
		}
		root.setAttribute( 'data-edminboost-ready', 'true' );
	} );
} )();
```

`edminboostData` shape: `{ version: string, strings: { ready: string } }`.

## CSS (`admin/css/`)

- Prefix all selectors with `.edminboost-` to avoid admin conflicts.
- Layout: `.edminboost-wrap`, `.edminboost-dashboard`, `.edminboost-card`, `.edminboost-status`.
- Dashboard: `.edminboost-feature-list`, `.edminboost-steps`.
- Settings form: `.edminboost-fieldset`, `.edminboost-checkbox-row`, `.edminboost-checkbox-grid`.
- Status modifiers: `.is-active`, `.is-inactive`.
- Responsive: feature list stacks at `max-width: 782px`.

## Partials (`admin/partials/`)

- `edminboost-admin-page.php` — dashboard overview (status, feature list, getting started).
- `edminboost-settings-features.php` — feature toggle fields (`EDMINBOOST_Admin::render_features_field()`).
- Use `fieldset` + `legend` for grouped settings; label every input.

## Enqueuing

`EDMINBOOST_Admin::enqueue_scripts()` / `enqueue_styles()` — only on plugin screens (`is_plugin_screen()`), version `EDMINBOOST_VERSION`. Handle: `edminboost-admin`.
